# Who reviews what in the guide.
#
# A page about how a team works is reviewed by that team. Adding a
# section here is the easiest way to get the right people onto a pull
# request automatically, rather than remembering to tag them.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, and a match replaces the owners rather
# than adding to them, so a section below is reviewed by its team alone.
# @rladies/website keeps everything not listed - layouts, config, the
# theme - and CI covers what they used to check by eye: check-build
# fails on a Hugo error, link-check catches broken links, i18n-check
# reports missing translations, and Netlify posts a preview.

*                                       @rladies/website

# Global team operations: one rule per team that runs the thing described
content/global-team/monitoring/         @rladies/chapter-activity
content/global-team/onboarding/         @rladies/chapter-onboarding
